@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``::
+
+    >>> console.out("Hello", "World!", sep=", ")
+
+Unlike print and log, ``out`` does not pretty print containers or objects, does not word wrap or crop output to the console width, and does not process console markup or emoji codes. Square brackets and emoji codes are written literally.
+
+``out`` supports a basic ``style`` and automatic highlighting. Highlighting is on by default; pass ``highlight=False`` to disable it, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting. Use ``out`` when you want raw text output, and print or log for rich formatting.
+
+
